Q: Centered ScrollView content doesn&#39;t return to position after pull-to-refresh with a large navigation title in SwiftUI A: <p>It may be the modifier <code>.containerRelativeFrame</code> that is causing this problem. For content inside a <code>ScrollView</code>, the &quot;container&quot; is the <code>ScrollView</code>, but I am guessing that the size may change when a refresh is being performed and the activity indicator is showing.</p>
<p>I would suggest using a <code>GeometryReader</code> to measure the size of the area occupied by the <code>ScrollView</code>. Then, set this size as the minimum size for the <code>VStack</code>. This way, the modifier <code>.containerRelativeFrame</code> is not needed.</p>
<p>You said you tried using a <code>GeometryReader</code> already and it didn't work. However, you didn't show how you tried it. Give it a try as follows:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>NavigationStack {
    GeometryReader { geo in
        ScrollView(.vertical) {
            VStack(spacing: 30) {
                // ...
            }
            .frame(minWidth: geo.size.width, minHeight: geo.size.height)
        }
    }
    .refreshable {
        try? await Task.sleep(for: .seconds(2))
    }
    .navigationTitle(&quot;Title&quot;)
}
</code></pre>
